Files this licence does not cover

The files named below are fonts with the data and documents that travel
with them, and copies of other projects' code. They are not licensed under
CC BY-NC-SA 4.0. Each is distributed under its own licence, which sits
beside it in the same directory. For the fonts the SIL Open Font License 1.1
requires this: "The Font Software, modified or unmodified, in part or in
whole, must be distributed entirely under this license, and must not be
distributed under any other license" (condition 5).

Fonts embedded in the baud application:

  baud-app/fonts/jetbrains-mono/
      JetBrains Mono 2.304, unmodified: SIL Open Font License 1.1
      (OFL.txt, AUTHORS.txt).
  baud-app/fonts/stix-two-math/
      STIX Two Math 2.13 b171, unmodified: SIL Open Font License 1.1
      (OFL.txt).
  baud-app/fonts/symbols-nerd-font/
      Symbols Nerd Font Mono 3.5.1, unmodified: MIT (LICENSE), with the icon
      sets it carries under their own licences, which README.md lists and
      icon-licences/ holds, copied from nerd-fonts v3.5.1 src/glyphs/: SIL
      Open Font License 1.1 (Pomicons, Weather Icons, and Font Awesome, whose
      licence applies the OFL to its icons packaged as fonts), Apache 2.0
      (Material Design), CC BY 4.0 (Codicons), the Unlicense (Font Logos)
      and MIT (Octicons and the rest).
  baud-app/fonts/built/Regular.ttf
  baud-app/fonts/built/Bold.ttf
      and OFL.txt, FONTLOG.txt and AUTHORS.txt beside them: JetBrains Mono
      with Hebrew drawn from Cascadia Mono, a Modified Version under the SIL
      Open Font License 1.1 (OFL.txt, which carries both copyright lines).
  baud-app/fonts/glyphs/languages/hebrew/CascadiaMono.ttf
  baud-app/fonts/glyphs/languages/hebrew/anchors-400.json
  baud-app/fonts/glyphs/languages/hebrew/anchors-700.json
      Cascadia Mono from Cascadia Code v2407.24, and data read out of it
      (the anchors files under OFL.txt as SOURCE states, pending the call
      below): SIL Open Font License 1.1, as its repository's LICENSE states
      (OFL.txt, SOURCE).

  Three questions about these files are open, and this section does not
  answer them; baud-app/fonts/built/FONTLOG.txt records the first two. The
  Cascadia release binary's own name table carries a notice that differs from
  its repository's licence. Whether the Hebrew build modules (the files under
  baud-app/fonts/glyphs/languages/hebrew/build/, and casanchors.py beside
  them) are Font Software under the OFL or code under this licence has not
  been decided, nor whether anchors-400.json and anchors-700.json, data read
  out of Cascadia Mono, are: hebrew/SOURCE states them under OFL.txt and the
  licence call is to confirm it. And baud-font/tests/var/outlines.txt,
  outlines of JetBrains Mono's and Fira Code's variable fonts written by
  scripts/gvar-oracle.py, may be part of the Font Software under OFL
  condition 5; this section names it under neither licence. The same holds
  for baud-font/tests/var/cff2-outlines.txt, outlines of Source Code VF
  written by scripts/cff2-oracle.py.

Fonts the tests read:

  baud-font/tests/fonts/BungeeTint-Regular.ttf
      SIL Open Font License 1.1 (BungeeTint-LICENSE.txt).
  baud-font/tests/fonts/FiraCode-Regular.ttf
  baud-font/tests/fonts/FiraCode-VF.ttf
      SIL Open Font License 1.1 (FiraCode-LICENSE.txt).
  baud-font/tests/fonts/JetBrainsMono-Regular.ttf
  baud-font/tests/fonts/JetBrainsMono-Variable.ttf
  baud-font/tests/fonts/JetBrainsMono-Italic-Variable.ttf
      SIL Open Font License 1.1 (JetBrainsMono-LICENSE.txt).
  baud-font/tests/fonts/NotoColorEmoji-subset.ttf
      A subset of Noto Color Emoji, a Modified Version under the SIL Open
      Font License 1.1 (NotoColorEmoji-LICENSE.txt).
  baud-font/tests/fonts/SourceCodeVF-Upright.otf
      SIL Open Font License 1.1, Reserved Font Name 'Source'
      (SourceCodeVF-LICENSE.txt); unmodified.
  baud-font/tests/var/bake/JetBrainsMono-Variable-400.ttf
  baud-font/tests/var/bake/JetBrainsMono-Variable-700.ttf
  baud-font/tests/var/bake/JetBrainsMono-Italic-Variable-400.ttf
  baud-font/tests/var/bake/JetBrainsMono-Italic-Variable-700.ttf
      Instances of JetBrains Mono's variable fonts, Modified Versions under
      the SIL Open Font License 1.1 (JetBrainsMono-LICENSE.txt).

The other fonts under baud-font/tests/ were written from nothing by baud's
own scripts and are under this licence: sbix-strikes.ttf, cblc-cases.ttf,
gvar-cases.ttf, cff2-cases.otf, the cases fonts in var/bake/ and everything
in var/hvar/.

Other projects' code:

  Lines ported from other projects into baud's files keep their own
  licence: the test helper sfte in baud-render/src/trail.rs, from sfte
  (zlib; LICENSES/sfte-Zlib.txt); two test helpers in
  baud-core/tests/image_geometry.rs, from yazi (MIT; LICENSES/yazi-MIT.txt);
  the OKLab conversions and the gamut clip in baud-render/src/color.rs,
  from Björn Ottosson's published code (MIT; LICENSES/ottosson-MIT.txt);
  and the Xcms conversions in baud-domain/src/vt/xcms.rs and the CRT data
  in baud-domain/src/vt/xcms/tests.rs, from libX11 (Tektronix's TekHVC
  and Xcms notices and The Open Group's; LICENSES/libx11-xcms.txt).

Third-party research sources:

  docs/research/sources/
      Copies of other people's documents and code that baud's research
      cites, each under its own terms; this licence covers none of them.
      THIRD_PARTY.md lists every file with its licence, where its notice is
      and where it came from, and names those that carry no grant to
      redistribute; the licence texts are in LICENSES/. The owner's own
      observations there (the *-observed/ directories) are under this
      licence, except for the third-party artwork the screenshots show:
      Apple Color Emoji and other system fonts' glyphs stay their owners',
      and THIRD_PARTY.md names each screenshot that shows them.
